<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Analisa TV - Help & Instructions</title>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Space+Mono:wght@400;700&family=Orbitron:wght@400;700;900&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <style>
        /* =====================================================
           Everything is scoped under .help-page so the styles
           never leak into the host page this is injected into.
           ===================================================== */

        .help-page {
            --gold: #daa520;
            --gold-light: #ffd700;
            --gold-dark: #b8860b;
            --bg-dark: #0a0a0f;
            --panel: rgba(28, 28, 38, 0.9);
            --text: #f0f0f0;
            --text-muted: #ccc;
            --text-dim: #aaa;
            --danger: #ff5555;
            --font-display: 'Orbitron', sans-serif;
            --font-body: 'Space Mono', monospace;

            /* Own full-screen scroll container: immune to the host's
               flex centering, so the top of the page is always reachable. */
            position: fixed;
            inset: 0;
            overflow-x: hidden;
            overflow-y: scroll;
            color: var(--text);
            font-family: var(--font-body);
            line-height: 1.6;
            background: rgba(10, 10, 15, 0.35);
            scrollbar-width: thin;
            scrollbar-color: var(--gold) var(--bg-dark);
        }

        .help-page * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }

        /* ---------- Custom scrollbar ---------- */
        .help-page::-webkit-scrollbar { width: 14px; height: 14px; }

        .help-page::-webkit-scrollbar-track {
            background: var(--bg-dark);
            border-left: 1px solid rgba(218, 165, 32, 0.2);
        }

        .help-page::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb {
            background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--gold-light) 0%, var(--gold) 50%, var(--gold-dark) 100%);
            border: 3px solid var(--bg-dark);
            border-radius: 999px;
        }

        .help-page::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb:hover {
            background: linear-gradient(180deg, #fff2a8 0%, var(--gold-light) 50%, var(--gold) 100%);
            box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(218, 165, 32, 0.6);
        }

        .help-page::-webkit-scrollbar-corner { background: var(--bg-dark); }

        .help-page .container {
            max-width: 1200px;
            margin: 0 auto;
            padding: 2rem;
        }

        /* ---------- Back button ---------- */
        .help-page .back-btn {
            position: fixed;
            top: 1rem;
            left: 1rem;
            z-index: 100;
            display: inline-flex;
            align-items: center;
            gap: 0.5rem;
            padding: 0.6rem 1.1rem;
            background: rgba(10, 10, 15, 0.85);
            color: var(--gold);
            border: 1px solid rgba(218, 165, 32, 0.5);
            border-radius: 999px;
            font-family: var(--font-display);
            font-size: 0.85rem;
            font-weight: 700;
            letter-spacing: 1px;
            text-decoration: none;
            cursor: pointer;
            backdrop-filter: blur(6px);
            transition: all 0.25s ease;
        }

        .help-page .back-btn:hover,
        .help-page .back-btn:focus-visible {
            background: var(--gold);
            color: var(--bg-dark);
            box-shadow: 0 0 18px rgba(218, 165, 32, 0.45);
            outline: none;
        }

        /* ---------- Header ---------- */
        .help-page .header {
            text-align: center;
            margin: 3.5rem 0 3rem;
            padding-bottom: 2rem;
            border-bottom: 2px solid rgba(218, 165, 32, 0.3);
        }

        .help-page h1 {
            font-family: var(--font-display);
            font-size: 3rem;
            font-weight: 900;
            letter-spacing: 2px;
            margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
            background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--gold) 0%, var(--gold-light) 100%);
            -webkit-background-clip: text;
            background-clip: text;
            -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
        }

        .help-page .subtitle {
            color: #888;
            font-size: 1rem;
            letter-spacing: 1px;
            margin: 0;
        }

        /* ---------- Sections ---------- */
        .help-page .section {
            background: var(--panel);
            border: 1px solid rgba(218, 165, 32, 0.2);
            border-radius: 12px;
            padding: 2rem;
            margin-bottom: 2rem;
            transition: border-color 0.3s ease;
        }

        .help-page .section:hover { border-color: rgba(218, 165, 32, 0.4); }

        .help-page h2 {
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            gap: 0.75rem;
            font-family: var(--font-display);
            font-size: 1.8rem;
            color: var(--gold);
            margin-bottom: 1rem;
        }

        .help-page h2 .icon { font-size: 2rem; }

        .help-page h3 {
            font-family: var(--font-display);
            font-size: 1.2rem;
            color: var(--gold-light);
            margin: 1.5rem 0 0.75rem;
        }

        .help-page p {
            color: var(--text-muted);
            margin-bottom: 1rem;
        }

        /* ---------- Feature grid ---------- */
        .help-page .feature-grid {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr));
            gap: 1.5rem;
            margin-top: 1.5rem;
        }

        .help-page .feature-card {
            background: rgba(10, 10, 15, 0.6);
            border: 1px solid rgba(218, 165, 32, 0.2);
            border-radius: 8px;
            padding: 1.5rem;
            transition: all 0.3s ease;
        }

        .help-page .feature-card:hover {
            border-color: var(--gold);
            transform: translateY(-3px);
            box-shadow: 0 5px 20px rgba(218, 165, 32, 0.2);
        }

        .help-page .feature-card h4 {
            font-family: var(--font-display);
            font-size: 1rem;
            color: var(--gold);
            margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
        }

        .help-page .feature-card p {
            font-size: 0.85rem;
            color: var(--text-dim);
            margin: 0;
        }

        /* ---------- Tip & warning boxes ---------- */
        .help-page .tip-box {
            background: rgba(218, 165, 32, 0.1);
            border-left: 4px solid var(--gold);
            border-radius: 4px;
            padding: 1rem 1.5rem;
            margin: 1.5rem 0;
        }

        .help-page .tip-box strong { color: var(--gold-light); }

        .help-page .warning {
            background: rgba(255, 85, 85, 0.1);
            border-left: 4px solid var(--danger);
            border-radius: 4px;
            padding: 1rem 1.5rem;
            margin: 1.5rem 0;
            color: #ffaaaa;
        }

        /* ---------- Numbered steps ---------- */
        .help-page .step-list {
            list-style: none;
            counter-reset: step-counter;
            margin: 1.5rem 0;
        }

        .help-page .step-list li {
            counter-increment: step-counter;
            position: relative;
            margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
            padding-left: 3rem;
            color: var(--text-muted);
        }

        .help-page .step-list li::before {
            content: counter(step-counter);
            position: absolute;
            left: 0;
            top: 0;
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            width: 2rem;
            height: 2rem;
            border-radius: 50%;
            background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--gold) 0%, var(--gold-dark) 100%);
            color: var(--bg-dark);
            font-family: var(--font-display);
            font-weight: 700;
        }

        .help-page .step-list li strong {
            display: block;
            color: var(--text);
        }

        /* ---------- FAQ ---------- */
        .help-page .faq-item {
            margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
            padding-bottom: 1.5rem;
            border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
        }

        .help-page .faq-item:last-child {
            margin-bottom: 0;
            padding-bottom: 0;
            border-bottom: none;
        }

        .help-page .faq-question {
            color: var(--gold-light);
            font-weight: 700;
            margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
        }

        .help-page .faq-answer {
            color: var(--text-dim);
            padding-left: 1.5rem;
        }

        .help-page .faq-answer ul {
            list-style: none;
            margin-top: 0.5rem;
        }

        .help-page .faq-answer li::before {
            content: "• ";
            color: var(--gold);
        }

        /* ---------- Badges ---------- */
        .help-page .badge {
            display: inline-block;
            margin: 0.25rem;
            padding: 0.25rem 0.75rem;
            background: rgba(218, 165, 32, 0.2);
            color: var(--gold);
            border: 1px solid rgba(218, 165, 32, 0.3);
            border-radius: 20px;
            font-size: 0.75rem;
        }

        /* ---------- Footer ---------- */
        .help-page .footer {
            text-align: center;
            padding: 1rem 0 2rem;
        }

        .help-page .footer p {
            color: #666;
            font-size: 0.85rem;
            margin: 0;
        }

        /* ---------- Responsive ---------- */
        @media (max-width: 768px) {
            .help-page h1 { font-size: 2rem; }
            .help-page h2 { font-size: 1.4rem; }
            .help-page .container { padding: 1rem; }
            .help-page .section { padding: 1.5rem; }
            .help-page .header { margin-top: 4rem; }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="help-page">
    <a href="#" id="backBtn" class="back-btn" aria-label="Go back">&larr; Back</a>

    <div class="container">

        <header class="header">
            <h1>📺 ANALISA TV</h1>
            <p class="subtitle">Your Interactive Multi-Room Entertainment Hub</p>
        </header>

        <!-- WELCOME -->
        <section class="section">
            <h2><span class="icon">👋</span> Welcome!</h2>
            <p>Welcome to Analisa TV - your all-in-one interactive media and entertainment center for Second Life! Stream YouTube videos, listen to drop-free proxy radio stations, share live gameplay via WebRTC, display Flickr galleries, and play real-time socket multiplayer games with friends in your parcel.</p>
            <div class="tip-box">
                <strong>💡 First Time Here?</strong> Simply click the TV screen in Second Life to establish an LSL Handshake and launch the UI! The menu is simple and intuitive - everything you need is one click away.
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- HOW TO USE -->
        <section class="section">
            <h2><span class="icon">🎮</span> How to Use</h2>

            <h3>Getting Started</h3>
            <ol class="step-list">
                <li><strong>Click the TV Prim</strong>Initiates the secure LSL Handshake and loads the main system menu.</li>
                <li><strong>Select Media or Game Mode</strong>Pick from YouTube, Music, Radio, WebRTC Streaming, Flickr, or Multiplayer Games.</li>
                <li><strong>Enjoy Synchronized Playback</strong>Content streams seamlessly and synchronizes in real time for everyone in the room.</li>
            </ol>

            <h3>Multi-Room State Synchronization</h3>
            <p>Powered by Socket.IO, when someone changes a song, video, or starts a multiplayer game round, <strong>everyone connected to that room sees the exact same state in real time</strong>. It's like watching TV together!</p>

            <div class="tip-box">
                <strong>💡 Pro Tip:</strong> Neighboring parcels are isolated into separate channels so your playback won't interfere with adjacent land! Some venues may also restrict control to specific users or staff. If you can't change channels, enjoy the content being shared!
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- FEATURES -->
        <section class="section">
            <h2><span class="icon">✨</span> What's Available</h2>

            <div class="feature-grid">
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <h4>📺 YouTube</h4>
                    <p>Watch any YouTube video. Search keyword tags, paste a link, or enter a Channel ID!</p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <h4>🎵 Music</h4>
                    <p>Stream music from various sources. Perfect for parties and events!</p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <h4>🎬 Movies</h4>
                    <p>Browse and watch movies together. Great for movie nights!</p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <h4>📻 Radio</h4>
                    <p>Listen to live Shoutcast & Icecast stations from around the world, proxied to avoid HTTPS drops.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <h4>📸 Flickr</h4>
                    <p>Photo slideshows and explorer: search tags, inspect User/Group IDs, and set photos as TV wallpaper.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <h4>📡 Live TV</h4>
                    <p>Watch live television channels and streams.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <h4>🎮 Games</h4>
                    <p>Multiplayer games with others: Quiz Trivia, True/Myth, Who Am I?, This or That, and Chess!</p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <h4>🌐 Browser</h4>
                    <p>Browse websites directly on the TV screen.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <h4>🎥 Game Streaming</h4>
                    <p>Watch live game streams and esports, or share your own screen with low-latency WebRTC.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <h4>🗺️ Second Life</h4>
                    <p>Explore destination guides and landmarks, and receive direct teleport SLURLs in chat.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <h4>📺 Watch Together</h4>
                    <p>Synchronized viewing with Kosmi and CyTube platforms.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <h4>🎁 Freebies</h4>
                    <p>Discover free items, hunts and content in Second Life.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="tip-box">
                <strong>🔒 Protected Access:</strong> Adult and restricted content is password-protected. Ask the venue owner for the password.
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- WATCH TOGETHER -->
        <section class="section">
            <h2><span class="icon">🤝</span> Watch Together</h2>
            <p>The Watch Together feature gives you synchronized viewing options:</p>

            <h3>Built-in Sync System</h3>
            <p>Our native streaming system with real-time synchronization. Perfect for live events and performances.</p>

            <h3>Kosmi Integration</h3>
            <p>Watch YouTube, Netflix, Prime Video together, plus screen sharing and built-in games. Great for movie nights!</p>

            <h3>CyTube</h3>
            <p>Join a CyTube channel for synchronized playback with other viewers.</p>

            <div class="tip-box">
                <strong>💡 How it works:</strong> One person creates or joins a room, and everyone watches the same content at exactly the same time. It's like being in the same room watching the same screen!
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- SETTINGS -->
        <section class="section">
            <h2><span class="icon">🛠️</span> On-Screen Settings</h2>
            <p>Customize how your TV looks and behaves from the On Screen Settings panel. Each tab has its own controls, and most tabs include a reset button (Factory Default or Reset Lights to Normal).</p>

            <div class="feature-grid">
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <h4>🎨 Design & Style</h4>
                    <p>Pick a stand model, TV texture and back color. Set stand or wall mode, adjust back and webscreen transparency, and show or hide the frame.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <h4>📐 Shape & Size</h4>
                    <p>Scale the TV in 1% to 20% steps or use the House, Outside and Cinema presets. Choose an aspect ratio from 1:1 up to 32:9 ultrawide.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <h4>💡 Ambilight & Neon</h4>
                    <p>Switch the light and neon on, off or cycle them. Set the mood (Active, Normal, Cozy), glow color, intensity, range, fall and glow.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <h4>🔒 Security & Alarm</h4>
                    <p>Enable the house alarm, lock the TV to the owner, and show or hide the navigation bar.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="tip-box">
                <strong>💡 Lock TV:</strong> Locking the TV restricts browser access and playback controls exclusively to the device owner.
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- TIPS -->
        <section class="section">
            <h2><span class="icon">💡</span> Tips & Tricks</h2>

            <div class="faq-item">
                <div class="faq-question">🎯 Best Viewing Experience</div>
                <div class="faq-answer">Position your camera to face the TV screen directly. Use Alt+Click to zoom in for a better view!</div>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">
                <div class="faq-question">🎛️ Viewer Setup & Sound Preferences</div>
                <div class="faq-answer">
                    In Firestorm, go to <strong>Preferences → Sound & Media → Media</strong> and enable:
                    <ul>
                        <li>Media Auto-Play</li>
                        <li>Allow Inworld Scripts to Play Media</li>
                        <li>Play Media Attached to Other Avatars</li>
                    </ul>
                    In other viewers, enable "Play media attached to primitives" under Preferences → Sound & Media.
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">
                <div class="faq-question">🔊 No Sound or Stream Interrupted?</div>
                <div class="faq-answer">Ensure media is unmuted in your viewer top toolbar and check your system volume. If audio drops, our Node.js server automatically proxies audio streams to prevent HTTPS mixed-content blockages.</div>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">
                <div class="faq-question">⚡ Laggy Video?</div>
                <div class="faq-answer">Lower your graphics settings or move closer to the TV. The TV streams at 1280x720 resolution for optimal performance.</div>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">
                <div class="faq-question">🌐 Browser Not Loading?</div>
                <div class="faq-answer">Some viewers have stricter security settings. Try allowing the TV's URL in your viewer preferences under "Whitelist".</div>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">
                <div class="faq-question">⚡ Out of Sync with Room Viewers?</div>
                <div class="faq-answer">Hover at the top edge of the TV screen and click the 'Back' or 'Sync' button to realign your Socket.IO connection.</div>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">
                <div class="faq-question">👥 Multiple Viewers</div>
                <div class="faq-answer">Everyone in the same "room" sees the same content. If you want a private viewing experience, make sure you're in a unique room ID.</div>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">
                <div class="faq-question">📱 Control from Anywhere</div>
                <div class="faq-answer">Once you've opened the TV menu in your browser, you can control it even if you walk away from the TV object!</div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- TROUBLESHOOTING -->
        <section class="section">
            <h2><span class="icon">🔧</span> Troubleshooting</h2>

            <h3>TV Screen is Black</h3>
            <p><strong>Solution:</strong> Make sure "Play media attached to primitives" is enabled in your viewer settings. Right-click the TV and select "Play".</p>

            <h3>Can't Click the TV</h3>
            <p><strong>Solution:</strong> The TV might be locked to specific users. Contact the venue owner or staff.</p>

            <h3>Menu Not Opening</h3>
            <p><strong>Solution:</strong> Check if popups are blocked in your browser. Allow popups from this domain.</p>

            <h3>Video Playing But No Picture</h3>
            <p><strong>Solution:</strong> Refresh the TV by clicking it again. The source might have been removed or is unavailable.</p>

            <h3>Out of Sync with Others</h3>
            <p><strong>Solution:</strong> Refresh your browser or re-click the TV. You might be in a different room than other viewers.</p>

            <div class="warning">
                <strong>⚠️ Still Having Issues?</strong><br>
                Contact the venue owner or staff. They can reset the TV system or help with specific configuration issues.
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- TECHNICAL -->
        <section class="section">
            <h2><span class="icon">⚙️</span> Technical Information</h2>

            <h3>System Specs</h3>
            <p>
                <span class="badge">Resolution: 1280×720</span>
                <span class="badge">Real-time Socket.IO Sync</span>
                <span class="badge">Multi-room Support</span>
                <span class="badge">Node.js Engine</span>
                <span class="badge">WebRTC P2P</span>
                <span class="badge">Anti-Hibernation System</span>
            </p>

            <h3>Supported Browsers</h3>
            <p>The TV works best with modern browsers: Chrome, Firefox, Edge, Safari. Make sure your browser is up to date!</p>

            <h3>Second Life Viewers</h3>
            <p>Fully compatible with Firestorm, Official Second Life Viewer, and all modern CEF/Chromium-based viewers supporting Media on a Prim (MOAP).</p>

            <h3>Bandwidth Requirements</h3>
            <p>For smooth streaming, we recommend at least 5 Mbps download speed. HD content may require more.</p>
        </section>

        <!-- ETIQUETTE -->
        <section class="section">
            <h2><span class="icon">🤝</span> Viewing Etiquette</h2>

            <p><strong>Be Respectful:</strong> Remember that what you play affects everyone watching! Choose content appropriate for the venue and audience.</p>
            <p><strong>Ask Before Changing:</strong> If others are watching, it's polite to ask before changing the channel or video.</p>
            <p><strong>Volume Awareness:</strong> Your system volume affects only you, but consider that others might have different volume preferences.</p>
            <p><strong>Report Issues:</strong> If you encounter inappropriate content or technical problems, notify the venue staff.</p>
        </section>

        <!-- FOOTER -->
        <footer class="footer">
            <p>
                Analisa TV Ecosystem<br>
                Powered by Node.js & Socket.IO • Built for Second Life<br>
                For support, contact pedrosilva2014 in-world! 🎬✨<br>
                Enjoy your entertainment experience!
            </p>
        </footer>
    </div>

    <script>
    (function () {
        // Used only if the page is opened on its own (not inside the overlay).
        var FALLBACK_URL = '/';

        var btn = document.getElementById('backBtn');
        if (!btn) return;

        btn.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
            e.preventDefault();

            // Opened inside the main page: close the overlay and show the menu again.
            var overlay = document.getElementById('sub-content-overlay');
            if (overlay) {
                overlay.innerHTML = '';
                overlay.style.display = 'none';
                var grid = document.getElementById('main-grid');
                if (grid) grid.style.display = '';
                return;
            }

            // Opened standalone.
            if (window.history.length > 1) {
                window.history.back();
            } else {
                window.location.href = FALLBACK_URL;
            }
        });
    })();
    </script>
</div>
</body>
</html>
